    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Singles\" by Adam and the Ants is a comprehensive 20-track compilation released by Sony Music, chronicling the career-spanning A-sides from the band's punk and new wave era through Adam Ant's solo hits in rock and pop. Spanning from the 1978 debut \"Young Parisians\" to the 1995 track \"Wonderful,\" the collection is presented chronologically across CD or double red-and-white vinyl LP formats, roughly split between Adam & The Ants classics like \"Zerox,\" \"Kings of the Wild Frontier,\" \"Antmusic,\" \"Stand and Deliver,\" \"Prince Charming,\" and \"Ant Rap,\" and solo standouts such as \"Goody Two Shoes,\" \"Puss 'N Boots,\" \"Strip,\" \"Vive Le Rock,\" and \"Room at the Top.\"\n\nMusically, the set captures Adam Ant's evolution from raw, tribal punk with Burundi drum beats and eccentric tribal aesthetics in the Ants' material to polished, glam-infused pop-rock in his solo phase, blending catchy hooks, swaggering charisma, and provocative lyrics that defined early '80s UK chart dominance. Tracks like \"Dog Eat Dog\" and \"Apollo 9\" highlight the high-energy \"Antmusic\" style that propelled multiple No. 1 hits, while rarities such as the Decca-era \"Young Parisians\" offer punk roots rarely compiled on CD before.\n\nThis 2025 Sony U.K. release (with U.S. availability following) holds significance as an accessible entry point for fans and newcomers, reviving iconic singles without new liner notes but emphasizing Ant's restless creativity and transatlantic appeal, from UK chart-toppers to U.S. near-misses like \"Goody Two Shoes.\" Its punk-pop fusion remains influential, showcasing why Adam Ant endures as an '80s iconoclast.",
      "generated_at": "2026-02-01T13:53:50.502568",
      "model": "sonar",
      "source": "perplexity"
    }
